Why do some antivirus programs detect the file?

Some antivirus engines may flag the file as suspicious. This happens because the cheat uses techniques that can look similar to malware behavior.

For example:

injecting code into the game process (DLL injection)

modifying game memory

using the mod loader BepInEx

hooking and modifying functions

These techniques are commonly used by cheats and mods, so some antivirus engines may produce false positives.

Because of this, services like VirusTotal may show a few detections from heuristic or machine-learning based scanners.

The cheat itself does not contain malicious code and is only used to modify the game.






